  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has invented 111-minute Instant Noodles. As the name suggests, each packet takes exactly 111 minute to cook.\n\nChef's restaurant has XXX stoves and only 111 packet can be cooked in a single stove at any minute.\n\nHow many customers can Chef serve in YYY minutes if each customer orders exactly 111 packet of noodles?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input contains two space-separated integers XXX and YYY — the number of stoves and the number of minutes, respectively.\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nPrint a single integer, the **maximum** number of customers Chef can serve in YYY minutes",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤X,Y≤10001 \\leq X, Y \\leq 10001≤X,Y≤1000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3 7",
        "output": "21",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef cooks for Y=7Y = 7Y=7 minutes and can cook X=3X = 3X=3 packets per minute, one on each stove.\nSo, the total number of packets that can be cooked is X⋅Y=3⋅7=21X \\cdot Y = 3 \\cdot 7 = 21X⋅Y=3⋅7=21.\nEach person orders one packet, so the maximum number of customers that can be served is 212121."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "7 8",
        "output": "56",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef cooks for Y=8Y = 8Y=8 minutes and can cook X=7X = 7X=7 packets per minute, one on each stove.\nSo, the total number of packets that can be cooked is X⋅Y=7⋅8=56X \\cdot Y = 7 \\cdot 8 = 56X⋅Y=7⋅8=56.\nEach person orders one packet, so the maximum number of customers that can be served is 565656."
      }
    ]
  },
